Q: How do you make nth-child count children over multiple sibling elements? A: <p>Just apply<code>nth-child</code>to the first member of the descendant selector, not the last one.</p>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>div:nth-of-type(odd) &gt; div {
  color: red;
}
div:nth-of-type(even) &gt; div {
  color: blue;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="myDiv"&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    I want to be red.
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm some other content on the page&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="myDiv"&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    I want to be blue.
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
